  {
   "id": "commit:eb700003ebf3797af1de1f9e222478d6d7f7eea3",
   "type": "commit",
   "attributes": [
    {
     "name": "ref",
     "time": "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z",
     "value": "refs/heads/connor4312/mcp-1"
    },
    {
     "name": "push_id",
     "time": "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z",
     "value": 23069857921
    },
    {
     "name": "commit_sha",
     "time": "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z",
     "value": "eb700003ebf3797af1de1f9e222478d6d7f7eea3"
    },
    {
     "name": "commit_index",
     "time": "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z",
     "value": 1
    },
    {
     "name": "commit_message",
     "time": "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z",
     "value": "mcp: initial hacking\n\nThis is some basic work to get MCP hooked up. It's enough to discover\nand establish connections to MCP servers on the machine with very very\nbasic commands to manage them:\n\n![](https://memes.peet.io/img/25-03-2220f93e-3d1f-41ab-867e-0b9ba616ec6f.mp4)\n\nRefs #242864\n\nThe McpRegistry registers both collections of servers (from various\nconfig files) and 'delegates', which is currently _only_ the node\nextension host but is pretty generic and so could point at other\nprocesses in the future. SSE could even be served from the renderer when\nwe aren't on a remote.\n\nIt wraps into IMcpServerConnection's, which do some basic connection\nmanagement and expose the McpServerRequestHandler which speaks JSON-RPC\nto the MCP server. This is wrapped into the IMcpServer which is the\ncomplete, stateful representation of the server. It does stuff like\ncaching discovered tools such that they can be viewed and controlled\neven when the MCP server isn't running.\n\nThe IMcpService is the 'public' entry for other VS Code features. Its\nAPI is very simple right now, exposing an observable of the available\nservers, which should be easy for chat to consume.\n\nStill need to get some good tests going, add proper and more discovery,\nand excercise currently-untested API. SSE is also a stub right now."
    },
    {
     "name": "commit_author_name",
     "time": "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z",
     "value": "Connor Peet"
    },
    {
     "name": "commit_author_email",
     "time": "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z",
     "value": "connor@peet.io"
    },
